      "writtenOn": "2022-07-07T17:13:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also, why should this be creating and returning a `std::vector` at all? It is known how big it is and this class is already mutating state and isn\u0027t cross thread safe anyway. If this class just held onto a `std::unique_ptr\u003cSkFontArguments::VariationPosition::Coordinate[]\u003e coords` and kept that up to date in `readControls` (it really is just a different layout for the data updated there) then this could just return an `SkSpan\u003cconst SkFontArguments::VariationPosition::Coordinate\u003e` pointing at that one internal copy of the data instead of allocating a new place to put the data each time. In fact the user wouldn\u0027t even need to call `getCoordinates` more than once since the underlying data would just be updated each time `readControls` is called. If the user wants a copy they can always make a copy, but I\u0027m guessing no user will want to.",
      "revId": "53902d51fd80e079a0c4998d649c47110c242764",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
